## 5. Monitoring & Data Collection

### 5.1 What to Collect

| **Data Type** | **How to Collect** | **Why It's Needed** |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Patrol Data** | SMART system; patrol forms | Track illegal activities; measure project effectiveness |
| **Wildlife Observations** | Camera traps; visual observations | Monitor key species; biodiversity conservation |
| **Forest Observations** | Field notes; photographs | Track forest conditions; deforestation and degradation |
| **Community Feedback** | Meeting records; surveys | Track community satisfaction; project impact |
| **Project Activities** | Activity logs; photographs | Demonstrate project implementation |

### 5.2 Data Recording Standards

- **All observations must be recorded** — if it's not recorded, it didn't happen
- **Use standardised forms** — to ensure consistency and completeness
- **Record dates, times, and locations** — for all observations
- **Take photographs** — wherever possible
- **Share data regularly** — with project management

### 5.3 SMART Monitoring

SMART (Spatial Monitoring and Reporting Tool) is a software system for:
- Recording patrol observations
- Tracking illegal activities
- Managing protected area data
- Reporting on conservation outcomes

**Action:** Ensure all patrol teams are trained on SMART and using it consistently.

